We recieved some intial help towards the over arching architecure of our
approach and the data structures we were planning on using during our 
design checkoff. After that, it was just the two of us collaborating on 
what approaches we thought were best. We used github for version control
and kept each other informed on the architecture of our respective parts
of the project.

D The files that you provided and a short description of what each file 
is and its purpose

hashMap.h - the header file for the hashMap class which stores every
            instance of a word appearing in the provided directory

hashMap.cpp - the implementation file for the hashMap class

processing.h - the header file for the processor class which is used 
                to index the files and string lines

processing.cpp - the implementation file for the hashMap class

wrapper.h - the header file for the wrapper class which combines the 
            processor and hasMap

wrapper.cpp - the implementation for the wrapper class

main.cpp - the driver file of this program. It contains the query loop
            and nessecary file reading checks

unit_test.h - testing file that was used for processor and hashMap classes

README - this file, outlines and explains the presented program 


E How to compile and run your program

Running the "make" command will produce the gerp executable which can then
be run using this command format: "./gerp inputDirectory outputFile". 
inputDirectory is the directory you'd like to search through and outputFile
is the file where the answers to your queries will be stored. The following
are all supported query commands which you can use after running the step
above:

"word" - typing any string followed by the return key uses case sensitive 
search to look through the provided directory

@i "word" or @insensitive "word" - preceding a word by @i or @insensitive 
looks through the provided directory for that given word using case
insensitive search

@q or @quit or Ctrl + d - ends the program

@f newOutputFilename - closes the current outputfile and opens the new 
file for future query outputs to be written to


