H Details and an explanation of how you tested the various parts of your
classes and the program as a whole. You may reference the testing files 
that you submitted to aid in your explanation.

We started by building up the hashMap and processor files because that
they processor and store all the data that's used in queries later on.
We tested these classes using the provided unit testing framework. You
can find the specific tests in the unit_tests.h file. After words we 
built the wrapper and the query loop, which we tested using tinyData 
and the Gutenberg files and by passing various commands in. We tested
varioud edge cases like searching for an empty string using fully a
non-alpanumeric words, common words like the, different capitalizations
and mixtures of alphanumeric and non-alphanumeric characters, case 
insenitive search. After passing a specific edge-case commands through 
our implementation of gerp, we would diff the output file with the 
output file of the reference implementation ran with the same commands.


